{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-descending-properties-morphisms-fpqc}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6d914dd8cb65f080ba0a237168482dd190da07230f668bdf85b6e2b12a81302c", "source_text": "Properties of morphisms local in the fpqc topology on the target", "source_text_hash": "sha256:32b30f91ad208ea69e48112876108e9d3e150dc63c27005de852acbcd17f7339", "unit_id": "tag:02YJ:title"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{examples-section-non-descending-property-projective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8a0b20133a73dc9ce1346ef4d9a33cef231767644c10d5f5a294182a0352a5a0", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we find a large number of properties\nof morphisms of schemes which are local on the base\nin the fpqc topology. By contrast, in\nExamples, Section <REF_0001>\nwe will show that the properties ``projective'' and ``quasi-projective''\nare not local on the base even in the Zariski topology.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aebb9b220584ccf6dc2df630f1c7777427ff15c12f2baa82ec291d6beeb362a1", "unit_id": "tag:02YJ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-quasi-compact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c56e2622a2e095944bffaf4f1cdaf93a9606d26dda97950dc6dcb16d7f4b3556", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is quasi-compact''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:30c1ee8748d3036bd8d25b7d9a57d9a78363301d4c2bd0db7fa322ea6591bc71", "unit_id": "tag:02KQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0004": "$X'$", "MATH_0005": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-preserved-base-change}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-affine}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:76de086980049190ff664735c8f059dcc6c714a71cc02d6a5922341a18bd3e6f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9862e6aca817b929672b9bfe68c27cb7fdabde9ee42a143db25e061db9d7da8c", "source_text": "A base change of a quasi-compact morphism is quasi-compact, see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nBeing quasi-compact is Zariski local on the base, see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nFinally, let\n<MATH_0001> be a flat surjective morphism of affine schemes,\nand let <MATH_0002> be a morphism. Assume that the base change\n<MATH_0003> is quasi-compact. Then <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact,\nand <MATH_0005> is surjective. Hence <MATH_0006> is quasi-compact.\nThis implies that <MATH_0007> is quasi-compact.\nTherefore Lemma <REF_0003> applies and we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a79a241f7c5874fd43c5f2568fee08d61df76bfc4ed6bfd6797f20b46e7b5c9a", "unit_id": "tag:02KQ:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-quasi-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ac6df38263ca946a1784f7352489316987d68e57ea19fd8a7e4031f302c3f4c4", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is quasi-separated''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:449bdf8dd8987a7c0314b8f23d10b2f1d5a92af5a21c134efc6faf3cb33c2c8e", "unit_id": "tag:02KR:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta' : X' \\to X'\\times_{S'} X'$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Delta'$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta : X \\to X \\times_S X$", "MATH_0007": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-separated-permanence}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-characterize-quasi-separated}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-quasi-compact}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:faf349323a69d292e09e7baae3fefbbdece9a98c53419ba12145c8c66bda35c7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b27b647475736b98eacc84f51cf4d73127d80eb2fd9c0d47b1791f14d421f305", "source_text": "Any base change of a quasi-separated morphism is quasi-separated, see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nBeing quasi-separated is Zariski local on the base (from the\ndefinition or by\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nFinally, let\n<MATH_0001> be a flat surjective morphism of affine schemes,\nand let <MATH_0002> be a morphism. Assume that the base change\n<MATH_0003> is quasi-separated. This means that\n<MATH_0004> is quasi-compact.\nNote that <MATH_0005> is the base change of <MATH_0006>\nvia <MATH_0007>. By Lemma <REF_0003>\nthis implies <MATH_0008> is quasi-compact, and hence <MATH_0009> is\nquasi-separated.\nTherefore Lemma <REF_0004> applies and we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3118a01bc6b56b7b3dd22ddadeb3f0c75553c821c599a48319804e7358d85223", "unit_id": "tag:02KR:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-universally-closed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3865f395a9581706d03cb3366f59bf2ffa39ec362480a8798fdbdf8239a514b7", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is universally closed''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f44ff1cc9d6e4b9739244564d0b546b12b0f7ed7b89081db5bf814ba4c5c7667", "unit_id": "tag:02KS:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0004": "$T \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX' \\ar[d] &\nS' \\times_S T \\times_S X \\ar[d] \\ar[r] \\ar[l] &\nT \\times_S X \\ar[d] \\\\\nS' &\nS' \\times_S T \\ar[r] \\ar[l] &\nT\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0007": "$T$", "MATH_0008": "$S' \\times_S T$", "MATH_0009": "$X \\to S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-universally-closed-local-on-the-base}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-fpqc-quotient-topology}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87b90fe48f647d81b064eadffd311cdcc853e0ec161af8dc4c6c5c89b9f5a434", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d9372f6251d19f3c32f569f1d758a20b993bedefd35b4e318bad60ae9d5e019e", "source_text": "A base change of a universally closed morphism is universally closed\nby definition.\nBeing universally closed is Zariski local on the base (from the\ndefinition or by\nMorphisms, Lemma\n<REF_0001>).\nFinally, let\n<MATH_0001> be a flat surjective morphism of affine schemes,\nand let <MATH_0002> be a morphism. Assume that the base change\n<MATH_0003> is universally closed. Let <MATH_0004> be any morphism.\nConsider the diagram\n<MATH_0005>\nin which both squares are cartesian.\nThus the assumption implies that the middle vertical\narrow is closed. The right horizontal arrows are flat, quasi-compact\nand surjective (as base changes of <MATH_0006>).\nHence a subset of <MATH_0007> is closed if and only if its inverse\nimage in <MATH_0008> is closed, see Morphisms,\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nAn easy diagram chase shows that the right vertical\narrow is closed too, and we conclude <MATH_0009> is\nuniversally closed.\nTherefore Lemma <REF_0003> applies and we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a886170d98d0fc1943c6d5c420263c3e9447d8103b01b2eaecad6aee1fc77bd0", "unit_id": "tag:02KS:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-universally-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:91c0de8573127434b90874dc3a8d9e121ac5c69c6fd08b150285e253f620f9ed", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is universally open''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ae617e45a39c708dcd33c8722b9ce20a493ffcf12330cc6f3ad3a13c031dee28", "unit_id": "tag:02KT:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-universally-closed}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ab52f8d8c2d4d10d536253f23099a47966079455ef36f47d420ffeae920158cc", "source_text": "The proof is the same as the proof of\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:09354c69a5b49fb0efb079b54ac64f3d474be21a3ea61e9c1f9cc09ede48c831", "unit_id": "tag:02KT:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-universally-submersive}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d21b1509fa35d9b1d7e598fa7059d38b9d311800078a5f940941b25b2d182c86", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is universally submersive''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fe28d9fcd15c5639661ae0da141af29d7ad0d03ebcb376db3eb86be8b97ab848", "unit_id": "tag:0CEW:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-universally-closed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-fpqc-quotient-topology}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:740a1d55335bc000186ac625ca57de223fe36879d016fbbe84367b72c98adbf8", "source_text": "The proof is the same as the proof of\nLemma <REF_0001>\nusing that a quasi-compact flat surjective morphism is\nuniversally submersive by\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f134e89ff9754ddcaebe9bc775df821a05739238c155befa917343b85d1da51a", "unit_id": "tag:0CEW:proof"}
